{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340886",
      "title": "Making Sense of NextJS' Caching Types",
      "lectureOrder": 182,
      "videoOrder": 168,
      "sourceHash": "730c7ea6ab09270e7b1bbf92ce939bdd8f4668578a93a899e4c7f91d36c4c465",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 3.56,
          "en": "So, as mentioned before, Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.56,
          "end": 6.4,
          "en": "performs some pretty aggressive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.4,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.7,
          "end": 10.22,
          "en": "And to be precise, there are four",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.22,
          "end": 14.86,
          "en": "different areas where Next.js caches data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.86,
          "end": 16,
          "en": "or pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.34,
          "end": 20.12,
          "en": "Though I will also say that the amount of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.12,
          "end": 23.62,
          "en": "caching or the aggressiveness by which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.62,
          "end": 26.62,
          "en": "Next.js performs the caching will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.62,
          "end": 29.14,
          "en": "depend on the Next.js version you're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.14,
          "end": 29.66,
          "en": "using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.02,
          "end": 32.74,
          "en": "You get the most aggressive caching if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.74,
          "end": 34.88,
          "en": "you're using Next.js 14.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.38,
          "end": 37.84,
          "en": "And you can check your package.json",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.84,
          "end": 40,
          "en": "file to find out which version you're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.92,
          "end": 43.04,
          "en": "So you get the most aggressive caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.04,
          "end": 44.36,
          "en": "with Next.js 14.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.56,
          "end": 48.96,
          "en": "If you're using Next.js 15 or higher, it'll be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 48.96,
          "end": 52.2,
          "en": "a bit less aggressive because with Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 56.66,
          "en": "15, some caching behaviors and defaults",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.66,
          "end": 57.38,
          "en": "were changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.74,
          "end": 59.4,
          "en": "But I'll highlight the important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.4,
          "end": 62.44,
          "en": "differences as we explore the different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.44,
          "end": 63.44,
          "en": "kinds of caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 63.78,
          "end": 66.7,
          "en": "First, let me give you an overview of the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.7,
          "end": 69.26,
          "en": "different kinds of caching Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 69.26,
          "end": 70.42,
          "en": "performs for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.46000000000001,
          "en": "And that starts with request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.46000000000001,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "memoization, which is a fancy term",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 78.56,
          "en": "which in the end simply means that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.56,
          "end": 82.78,
          "en": "Next.js stores data requests with the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.78,
          "end": 85.82,
          "en": "same configuration so that duplicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.82,
          "end": 87.58,
          "en": "requests are avoided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.88,
          "end": 88.98,
          "en": "That's the main idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 89.96000000000001,
          "end": 93.32,
          "en": "And this request memoization only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 93.32,
          "end": 96.64,
          "en": "happens during one request that's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.64,
          "end": 99.42,
          "en": "being handled on the Next.js server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 99.8,
          "end": 103.18,
          "en": "This still might not be 100% clear, but I'll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.18,
          "end": 105.66,
          "en": "show you how request memoization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 105.66,
          "end": 107.97999999999999,
          "en": "works and what it means for you in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 107.97999999999999,
          "end": 111.03999999999999,
          "en": "detail at a concrete example in the next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.03999999999999,
          "end": 111.56,
          "en": "lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 111.75999999999999,
          "end": 112.28,
          "en": "No worries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 113.14,
          "end": 116.46000000000001,
          "en": "So there is this mechanism that simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 116.46000000000001,
          "end": 119.12,
          "en": "exists to make sure that duplicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 119.12,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "unnecessary requests to some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 123.4,
          "en": "source are avoided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 128.039,
          "en": "There also is a separate data cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 128.039,
          "end": 131.18,
          "en": "managed by Next.js which might sound",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 131.18,
          "end": 133.58,
          "en": "similar but which actually has a different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 133.58,
          "end": 134.14,
          "en": "purpose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 135.26,
          "end": 138.14,
          "en": "Where request memoization aims to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 138.14,
          "end": 140.76,
          "en": "avoid duplicate requests to a data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 140.76,
          "end": 143.16,
          "en": "source for a single request that's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 143.16,
          "end": 146.02,
          "en": "handled by the Next.js server, the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 146.02,
          "end": 149.14,
          "en": "cache is all about storing and reusing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 149.14,
          "end": 151.82,
          "en": "data that has been fetched from a data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 151.82,
          "end": 153.82,
          "en": "source if it hasn't changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "The idea behind this data cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.26,
          "end": 161.18,
          "en": "therefore is not to deduplicate requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 161.18,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "or avoid duplicate requests but instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 167.66,
          "en": "to avoid requests altogether unless the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.66,
          "end": 168.72,
          "en": "data has changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 170.6,
          "en": "Which of course means that your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.6,
          "end": 173.44,
          "en": "application may be a bit faster because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 173.44,
          "end": 176.04,
          "en": "those extra round trips to the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "source are avoided.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 178.28,
          "end": 181.52,
          "en": "And this data cache then persists until",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 181.52,
          "end": 185.6,
          "en": "it's revalidated manually by you and you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 185.6,
          "end": 187.94,
          "en": "will learn how to do that or after a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 187.94,
          "end": 190.6,
          "en": "certain time set by you and you will also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 190.6,
          "end": 191.68,
          "en": "learn how to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 195.76,
          "en": "In addition to caching data that might",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 195.76,
          "end": 199.3,
          "en": "be used by pages, Next.js also manages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 199.3,
          "end": 201.36,
          "en": "a full route cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.38,
          "end": 205.04,
          "en": "And the idea here is that Next.js does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 205.04,
          "end": 208.32,
          "en": "not just cache and store and reuse data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 208.32,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "that may be used by pages but instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 214.32,
          "en": "the entire page, the entire HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 214.32,
          "end": 217.07999999999998,
          "en": "and the entire React server component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 217.07999999999998,
          "end": 219.32,
          "en": "payload which is managed under the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 219.32,
          "end": 221.18,
          "en": "hood and which is used to render those",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 221.18,
          "end": 221.54,
          "en": "pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 222.7,
          "end": 225.34,
          "en": "This therefore does not just avoid extra",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.34,
          "end": 228.04,
          "en": "round trips to some data source but it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 228.04,
          "end": 230.7,
          "en": "instead entirely avoids the re-rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 230.7,
          "end": 233.88,
          "en": "of an entire HTML page and hence it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 233.88,
          "end": 236.18,
          "en": "speeds up pages even further because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 236.18,
          "end": 238.98,
          "en": "existing pages can be reused.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 239.32,
          "end": 240.22,
          "en": "That's the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 241.08,
          "end": 243.92,
          "en": "And this cache also persists until the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 243.92,
          "end": 246.38,
          "en": "related data cache is revalidated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 246.8,
          "end": 249.98,
          "en": "So when updated data is there, pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 249.98,
          "end": 252.98,
          "en": "also will be re-rendered but only then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 254.2,
          "end": 258.42,
          "en": "And then last but not least there is a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 258.42,
          "end": 259.519,
          "en": "router cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 260.18,
          "end": 262.84,
          "en": "And one key difference here is that all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 262.84,
          "end": 265.32,
          "en": "three other caches, request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "memoization, data cache and full route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 271.9,
          "en": "cache, all these caches are managed on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 271.9,
          "end": 272.82,
          "en": "the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 273.54,
          "end": 276.18,
          "en": "The router cache on the other hand is a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 276.18,
          "end": 278.26,
          "en": "cache that's managed on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 278.26,
          "end": 282.44,
          "en": "and here Next.js also stores some React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 282.44,
          "end": 285.06,
          "en": "server component payload in memory in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 285.06,
          "end": 287.54,
          "en": "the browser and it does that so that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 287.54,
          "end": 290.38,
          "en": "navigations between pages can happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 290.38,
          "end": 290.94,
          "en": "faster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 291.24,
          "end": 293.32,
          "en": "Because even with the full route cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 293.76,
          "end": 296.12,
          "en": "Next.js of course would need to send a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 296.12,
          "end": 299.76,
          "en": "request to the Next.js server to get that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 299.76,
          "end": 299.98,
          "en": "cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 300,
          "end": 302.5,
          "en": "cached page and that request to the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 302.5,
          "end": 305.64,
          "en": "server can be sped up or avoided if the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 305.64,
          "end": 308.12,
          "en": "page data is already managed on the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 308.12,
          "end": 310.2,
          "en": "client side and that's the idea behind the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 310.96,
          "en": "router cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 311.96,
          "end": 314.56,
          "en": "And this cache will be invalidated when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 314.56,
          "end": 318.42,
          "en": "new pages are rendered by the server or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 318.42,
          "end": 321.74,
          "en": "whenever you leave the Next.js rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 321.74,
          "end": 323.64,
          "en": "website and come back to it, for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 323.64,
          "end": 324.16,
          "en": "example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 325.06,
          "end": 327.6,
          "en": "So it's also worth noting that this router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 327.6,
          "end": 330.58,
          "en": "cache, this client-side router cache has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 330.58,
          "end": 333.58,
          "en": "been made a bit less aggressive with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 333.58,
          "end": 337.3,
          "en": "Next.js 15, simply to ensure that you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 337.3,
          "end": 340.96,
          "en": "don't run into weird situations where for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 340.96,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "some reason some page might not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 345.58,
          "en": "reflect your latest data when you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 345.58,
          "end": 346.72,
          "en": "expected it to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 346.98,
          "end": 349.26,
          "en": "But the feature still exists, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 349.26,
          "end": 351.86,
          "en": "also to speed up backward and forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 351.86,
          "end": 354.04,
          "en": "navigation if the user uses the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 354.04,
          "end": 355.659,
          "en": "appropriate buttons and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 356.92,
          "end": 359.52,
          "en": "So these are four different important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 359.52,
          "end": 362.36,
          "en": "caches managed by Next.js and if you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 362.36,
          "end": 365.08,
          "en": "wanna dive deeper there is an entire",
          "zh": ""
